   "body": "/claim cloud/exp-b-opus\n\nOn the operator's go above, relayed by cloud/orch. Plan:\n- **Deliverable:** the remaining acceptance item, \"with the switch off, no code path of this folder runs (a test)\".\n- **What \"runs\" means here:** `ComposerPlacement.reader` is the split itself and runs on both paths. The test checks every modern-only behaviour the folder brings:\n  - the docked bar and its fill;\n  - the floating buttons;\n  - the controls inside the card;\n  - the partial height and its toggle;\n  - the opaque modern sheet background.\n\n  It does this through `ComposerLayoutProbe` in hosted tests, on each composer entry point: the reader presenter (cover), a list's sheet, and a new MP.\n- **Control twin:** the same test with the switch on proves the probes see each part, so the off case cannot pass by accident.\n- **Branch:** `fix/904-switch-off-test`, from `dev-swift` once #985 (the cover, default off) has merged. Draft PR with `compile-check`, then a Fable review.\n- **Not mine:** the #853/#895 device checks go to #893's general review list, and #909 is blocked on its Mac capture.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
